@baseUrl = http://localhost:5274

### OpenAPI document
GET {{baseUrl}}/swagger/v1/swagger.json
Accept: application/json

### Health live
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/live
Accept: application/json

### Health ready
GET {{baseUrl}}/health/ready
Accept: application/json

### API without login should return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Accept: application/json

### Login employee
# @name loginEmployee
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "employee@top-uni.edu.pl",
  "password": "Employee123!"
}

### Get tickets with employee token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Get missing ticket - 404
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/9999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Create valid ticket - 201 Created
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Printer broken",
  "description": "Office printer not working"
}

### Create invalid ticket - 400 ProblemDetails
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": ""
}

### Update ticket status - PATCH
PATCH {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1/status
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "status": 1
}

### MVC create without anti-forgery token should be rejected
POST {{baseUrl}}/Tickets/Create
Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded

Title=CSRF test&Description=Request without token

### Security headers
GET {{baseUrl}}/
Accept: text/html

### Minimal API v2 - get all tickets
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/tickets
Accept: application/json

### Minimal API v2 - create ticket
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Ticket from Minimal API v2",
  "description": "Created during LAB 10"
}

### Minimal API v2 - validation error
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/tickets
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "",
  "description": ""
}

### Minimal API v2 - update missing ticket, ProblemDetails 404
PUT {{baseUrl}}/api/v2/tickets/9999
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "title": "Missing ticket",
  "description": "This should return ProblemDetails",
  "status": 1
}

### LAB 11 AMBITNE - protected Minimal API without token should return 401
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/tickets
Accept: application/json

### LAB 11 AMBITNE - protected Minimal API with employee token
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/tickets
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### LAB 11 AMBITNE - employee claim
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/tickets/me
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### LAB 11 AMBITNE - employee has allowed email domain
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/tickets/domain-resource
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Login outsider
# @name loginOutsider
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "outsider@unidesk.local",
  "password": "Outsider123!"
}

### LAB 11 AMBITNE - outsider wrong email domain should return 403
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/tickets/domain-resource
Authorization: Bearer {{loginOutsider.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### Login admin
# @name loginAdmin
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/ambitne/login
Content-Type: application/json
Accept: application/json

{
  "email": "admin@unidesk.local",
  "password": "Admin123!"
}

### LAB 11 STRETCH - normal user delete should return 403
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/1
Authorization: Bearer {{loginEmployee.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### LAB 11 STRETCH - admin delete should return 204 or 404
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/api/tickets/99999
Authorization: Bearer {{loginAdmin.response.body.$.accessToken}}
Accept: application/json

### LAB 12 AMBITNE - process diagnostics
GET {{baseUrl}}/diagnostics/process
Accept: application/json
